== Fiscal structure ==

The Balboan fiscal system is characterised by several structural features:

The tax base is narrow. Only 38.9% of the workforce pays income tax, and the top income bracket generates 42% of income tax revenue. The fiscal system is heavily dependent on the [[Estret (province)|Estret]] corridor and the [[Sant Cristòfor]] financial sector.

Canal revenue is fully allocated and does not contribute to the general fund. The redirect of $2.0 billion in canal revenue to debt service reduces borrowing requirements but limits fiscal flexibility.

The [[Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone|Free Trade Zone]]'s low-taxation financial hub strategy creates a structural tension: the financial sector generates approximately 35% of corporate profits but pays an effective rate of approximately 14%, shifting the tax burden to domestic manufacturing and petroleum.

Self-funding programmes — pensions, unemployment insurance, public housing, and hurricane response — operate outside the general fund through dedicated revenue sources, reducing the call on general revenue while maintaining major social programmes.

